{"domain":"D2","questionCount":9,"questions":[{"id":"imp-014","domain":"D2","task":"Determine technical preparation","topic":"Respiratory Signals","questionType":"Concept","difficulty":"Core","prompt":"Which signal is required to identify respiratory effort?","options":["Thermistor","Nasal pressure","Thoracoabdominal belts","Snore microphone"],"answer":"Thoracoabdominal belts","rationale":"Thoracoabdominal effort belts are the standard signals used to identify respiratory effort.","taskCode":"D2A","reportCategory":"Technical preparation and signal setup","referenceKeys":["brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","fundamentals","aast-psg","aasm-scoring-technical-specs","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","filter-sensitivity","aasm-scoring-current","aasm-scoring-adult-resp","respiratory-physiology-sleep"],"studyRecommendationKeys":["brpt-handbook","brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","fundamentals","aast-psg","aasm-scoring-technical-specs","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","filter-sensitivity","aasm-scoring-current","aasm-scoring-adult-resp","respiratory-physiology-sleep"]},{"id":"imp-027","domain":"D2","task":"Determine technical preparation","topic":"10-20 System","questionType":"Concept","difficulty":"Intermediate","prompt":"In the International 10-20 system, what is the distance from Fp1 to O1 if the total measurement from Nasion to Inion is 36 cm?","options":["3.6 cm","7.2 cm","18 cm","This cannot be calculated from the Nasion to Inion measurement alone."],"answer":"This cannot be calculated from the Nasion to Inion measurement alone.","rationale":"A single nasion-to-inion measurement does not provide enough information to calculate the diagonal distance from Fp1 to O1.","taskCode":"D2A","reportCategory":"Technical preparation and signal setup","referenceKeys":["brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","aasm-scoring-adult-staging","atlas-eeg-sleep","aasm-scoring-technical-specs","filter-sensitivity","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aasm-scoring-current"],"studyRecommendationKeys":["brpt-handbook","brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","fundamentals","aast-psg","aasm-scoring-technical-specs","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aasm-scoring-current","aasm-scoring-adult-staging","filter-sensitivity","atlas-eeg-sleep"]},{"id":"boost-024","domain":"D2","task":"Determine technical preparation","topic":"Electrode Placement","questionType":"Calculation","difficulty":"Advanced","prompt":"The head measurement from left to right preauricular point over the vertex is 34 cm. Approximately how far is the initial 10% mark from each preauricular point?","options":["1.7 cm","3.4 cm","6.8 cm","17 cm"],"answer":"3.4 cm","rationale":"Ten percent of 34 cm is 3.4 cm.","taskCode":"D2A","reportCategory":"Technical preparation and signal setup","referenceKeys":["brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","aasm-scoring-adult-staging","atlas-eeg-sleep","aasm-scoring-technical-specs","filter-sensitivity","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aasm-scoring-current"],"studyRecommendationKeys":["brpt-handbook","brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","fundamentals","aast-psg","aasm-scoring-technical-specs","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aasm-scoring-current","aasm-scoring-adult-staging","filter-sensitivity","atlas-eeg-sleep"]},{"id":"imp-031","domain":"D2","task":"Perform procedures and follow practice guidelines","topic":"MSLT","questionType":"Concept","difficulty":"Core","prompt":"During a Multiple Sleep Latency Test (MSLT), a Sleep Onset REM Period (SOREMP) is recorded when REM sleep occurs within how many minutes of sleep onset?","options":["10 minutes","15 minutes","20 minutes","30 minutes"],"answer":"15 minutes","rationale":"A SOREMP is scored when REM occurs within 15 minutes of sleep onset, and Version 3 adds a dedicated reporting section for MSLT and MWT.","taskCode":"D2B","reportCategory":"Study procedure and practice guidelines","referenceKeys":["brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","aasm-scoring-adult-staging","atlas-eeg-sleep","aasm-mslt-mwt","hypersomnia","report-math","fundamentals-testing","aast-psg-technical","aasm-s