","ETCO2 does not change breath to breath","ETCO2 is a DC signal and therefore timeless"],"answer":"The sampled gas must travel through tubing before being measured","rationale":"A transport delay occurs because exhaled gas is aspirated through tubing to the analyzer.","taskCode":"D2B","reportCategory":"Study procedure and practice guidelines","referenceKeys":["brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","oxygen-therapy-sleep","aast-abg","respiratory-physiology-sleep","fundamentals-testing","aast-psg-technical","aasm-mslt-mwt","aasm-scoring-hypoventilation"],"studyRecommendationKeys":["brpt-handbook","brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","fundamentals","aast-psg","aasm-mslt-mwt","infection","oxygen-therapy-sleep","aast-abg","fundamentals-testing","aast-psg-technical","aasm-scoring-hypoventilation","respiratory-physiology-sleep"]},{"id":"imp-017","domain":"D2","task":"Identify, respond, and document","topic":"Artifact Recognition","questionType":"Troubleshooting","difficulty":"Core","prompt":"Which artifact produces slow, rolling baseline drift?","options":["Muscle artifact","Electrode popping","Sweat artifact","60-Hz interference"],"answer":"Sweat artifact","rationale":"Sweat artifact typically appears as a slow, rolling baseline drift.","taskCode":"D2C","reportCategory":"Troubleshooting, safety, and documentation","referenceKeys":["brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","artifact-troubleshooting","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aast-psg-technical","patient-safety"],"studyRecommendationKeys":["brpt-handbook","brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","fundamentals","aast-psg","artifact-troubleshooting","ekg-tech-support","safety-emergency","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aast-psg-technical","patient-safety"]},{"id":"imp-006","domain":"D2","task":"Identify, respond, and document","topic":"Artifact Recognition","questionType":"Troubleshooting","difficulty":"Intermediate","prompt":"Which of the following is the most likely cause of high-frequency artifact across all EEG channels?","options":["Sweat artifact","Cardiac artifact","Electrode popping","Muscle tension"],"answer":"Muscle tension","rationale":"Diffuse high-frequency artifact across EEG channels is most consistent with muscle activity, not sweat drift or cardiac artifact.","taskCode":"D2C","reportCategory":"Troubleshooting, safety, and documentation","referenceKeys":["brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","artifact-troubleshooting","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aasm-scoring-technical-specs","filter-sensitivity","aast-psg-technical","patient-safety","ekg-tech-support","aasm-scoring-current"],"studyRecommendationKeys":["brpt-handbook","brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","fundamentals","aast-psg","artifact-troubleshooting","ekg-tech-support","safety-emergency","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aast-psg-technical","patient-safety","aasm-scoring-current"]},{"id":"boost-015","domain":"D2","task":"Identify, respond, and document","topic":"Artifact","questionType":"Troubleshooting","difficulty":"Advanced","prompt":"A sudden sharp transient appears at the same time in every derivation that uses one shared reference electrode. What is the most likely source?","options":["Single bad shared electrode","Normal vertex wave","REM burst","Snore artifact"],"answer":"Single bad shared electrode","rationale":"A problem in a shared electrode contaminates all derivations that include it.","taskCode":"D2C","reportCategory":"Troubleshooting, safety, and documentation","referenceKeys":["brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","artifact-troubleshooting","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aasm-scoring-technical-specs","filter-sensitivity","infection","aast-psg-technical","patient-safety"],"studyRecommendationKeys":["brpt-handbook","brpt-blueprint","brpt-refs","fundamentals","aast-psg","artifact-troubleshooting","ekg-tech-support","safety-emergency","fundamentals-signal-acquisition","aast-psg-technical","patient-safety"]}]}